<h1>🚀 Pulse | Personalized Content Dashboard</h1>
<p><strong>Software Development Engineer (SDE) Intern — Frontend Development Assignment Documentation</strong></p>

<div class="box">
  <p><strong>Project Name:</strong> Pulse - Personalized Content Dashboard<br>
  <strong>Technology Stack:</strong> Next.js 14 (App Router), React 18, TypeScript, Redux Toolkit, Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion, Vitest, Cypress<br>
  <strong>Developer:</strong> Frontend Engineering SDE Candidate</p>
</div>

<hr>

<h2>1. Executive Summary & Overview</h2>
<p>The <strong>Personalized Content Dashboard</strong> is a high-performance web application designed for users to track, interact with, and organize real-time content across multiple domains (Technology, Finance, Sports, Entertainment, Science, Health, Gaming). The application consolidates news articles, movie/music recommendations, and social media posts into a single interactive feed.</p>

<p>Key highlights include:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>State Management:</strong> Centralized Redux Toolkit store managing asynchronous thunks, user preferences, bookmarking, and local persistence.</li>
  <li><strong>Interactive UI/UX:</strong> Framer Motion drag-and-drop feed reordering, dark/light theme switching, and smooth modal media reader.</li>
  <li><strong>API Integration:</strong> Hybrid fetcher supporting live <code>NewsAPI</code> queries with keyless fallback mock generators.</li>
  <li><strong>Performance & Search:</strong> 300ms debounced search bar with instant cross-category search and grid/list view mode switching.</li>
  <li><strong>Testing Best Practices:</strong> Vitest unit test suite (100% passing) and Cypress E2E test specs.</li>
</ul>

<hr>

