<hr>

<h2>3. Detailed Feature Breakdown</h2>

<h3>3.1 Category Preferences & Persistent Settings</h3>
<p>Users can select their preferred content categories (e.g., <i>Technology, Finance, Sports</i>) via the sidebar or Settings modal. Preferences automatically save to <code>localStorage</code> and sync across browser sessions.</p>

<h3>3.2 Interactive Cards & Media Previews</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>News Cards:</strong> Reading time indicator, source badge, external article links.</li>
  <li><strong>Recommendation Cards:</strong> Interactive video trailer preview modal and audio stream controls.</li>
  <li><strong>Social Cards:</strong> User handles, verified badges, like button counter, and discussion thread simulator.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.3 Drag-and-Drop Feed Organization</h3>
<p>Each card contains an accessible drag handle. Using Framer Motion's <code>Reorder.Group</code> and <code>Reorder.Item</code>, users can reorder their content feed in real time without screen flickers.</p>

<h3>3.4 Real-Time Live Feed Simulator (WebSocket/SSE)</h3>
<p>A background WebSocket feed simulator streams live breaking updates every 12 seconds when enabled in Settings, triggering animated toast notifications and updating the unread notification badge.</p>

<h3>3.5 Multi-Language Internationalization (i18n)</h3>
<p>Includes built-in dictionary support for four languages: <strong>English (en)</strong>, <strong>Spanish (es)</strong>, <strong>French (fr)</strong>, and <strong>German (de)</strong>.</p>

<hr>

<h2>4. State Management (Redux Toolkit)</h2>

<pre>
store/
├── index.ts              # Configures root store and typed hooks (useAppDispatch, useAppSelector)
├── feedSlice.ts          # Manages item arrays, async status, active filters, search query & reordering
├── preferencesSlice.ts   # Manages categories, dark theme, view mode, language, & API keys
├── favoritesSlice.ts     # Manages bookmarked items and IDs persisted to localStorage
└── authSlice.ts          # Manages user profile information and mock authentication state
</pre>

<hr>

<h2>5. Testing Strategy & Results</h2>

<h3>5.1 Unit Testing (Vitest)</h3>
<p>Unit tests verify Redux slice reducers and state transitions under <code>src/test/</code>:</p>
<ul>
  <li><code>preferencesSlice.test.ts</code>: Tests category toggling, theme changes, view mode switching, and language updates.</li>
  <li><code>feedSlice.test.ts</code>: Tests search query setting, content-type filtering, card reordering, and real-time item prepending.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Result:</strong> <code>8 passed (8)</code> across 2 test files.</p>

<h3>5.2 End-to-End Testing (Cypress)</h3>
<p>Cypress E2E specs in <code>cypress/e2e/dashboard.cy.ts</code> test search debouncing, card bookmarking, settings drawer, and page routing.</p>

<hr>

<h2>6. Instructions to Run & Verify</h2>

<pre>
# 1. Install dependencies
npm install

# 2. Start local development server
npm run dev
# App opens at http://localhost:3000

# 3. Execute Vitest Unit Tests
npm run test

# 4. Production Build Verification
npm run build
npm run start
</pre>

